      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A child with a large ventricular aneurysm was completely free of symptoms when admitted to the hospital; a chest-x-ray previously performed because of acute pneumonia had evidenced a bulge of the left border of the heart. The diagnosis of left ventricular aneurysm was verified by left ventricular angiography. Selective coronary angiography and angiocardiography of the right heart were also performed."},
